{# THE SETTINGS SECTION OF THE PATROLS CONFIGURE PAGE — body only.

   NO HEAD, NO STRIP, NO CRUMB, NO WAY BACK. The shell draws all four; this file
   writes the section's content and nothing around it, which is the whole of what
   a rendered section is.

   TWO NUMBERS, AND NOTHING ELSE ON IT. The words a ranger picks from — the types,
   the stations, the observation kinds — each keep a section of their own in the
   strip above, so nothing about them is restated here and nothing here links out
   to them: the strip is how a person gets to a section.

   IT SPENDS ONLY THE PLATFORM'S VOCABULARY — .c, .frow, .fld, .staddrow — because
   the shell's stylesheet is the only one linked on the configure page, and
   because those classes are the shell's to define. A module that redefined one
   would be drift, and the conformance test says so. It is also why there is no
   index badge on the heading: the design draws one with a class no sheet here
   ships.

   BOTH FIELDS ARE OF ONE RECORD AND SAVE TOGETHER, so nothing here writes on
   change. → POST …/configure/settings (patrol_settings_save) #}

{% set save = patrol_url('patrol_settings_save', {uuid: area.uuid}) %}

{% if save %}<form method="post" action="{{ save }}">
<input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}">{% endif %}
<div class="c" style="margin-bottom:20px">
    <span class="tab">Thresholds<span class="src">· {{ settings.areaChose ? 'this area’s own' : 'the installation’s, until this area saves' }}</span></span>
    <p class="use">The two numbers the module runs on. The words a ranger picks from — the types, the stations, the
        observation kinds — each have a section of their own in the strip above.</p>
    <div class="frow">
        <label for="patrol-gap">gps gap</label>
        <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:9px">
            <input class="fld snum" id="patrol-gap" type="number" name="gap_threshold_minutes"
                   min="{{ minGapMinutes }}" max="{{ maxGapMinutes }}" value="{{ settings.gapThresholdMinutes }}"{{ save ? '' : ' disabled' }}>
            <span class="use" style="margin:0">minutes without a fix before a track is drawn as broken and the patrol is flagged for review.</span>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="frow">
        <label for="patrol-retention">discard keeps</label>
        <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:9px">
            <input class="fld snum" id="patrol-retention" type="number" name="discard_retention_days"
                   min="{{ minRetentionDays }}" max="{{ maxRetentionDays }}" value="{{ settings.discardRetentionDays }}"{{ save ? '' : ' disabled' }}>
            <span class="use" style="margin:0">days a discarded patrol stays recoverable before it is purged.</span>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

{% if save %}
    {# THE FORM ENDS WITH ITS OWN ACTIONS ON ONE HAIRLINE — the shell's
       `.staddrow`, the row the area's Stations configure card draws and the one
       idiom a configure form ends in. The quiet way out comes first and the
       accent last. It is NOT a way back off the section — the strip, the lit
       Configure and the crumb are those, and there are no others. #}
    <div class="staddrow">
        {% set out = patrol_url('patrol_dashboard', {uuid: area.uuid}) %}
        {% if out %}<a class="tgl" href="{{ out }}">Cancel</a>{% endif %}
        <button class="cta" type="submit">Save settings</button>
    </div>
</form>
{% endif %}
